## Request ID Middleware Implementation

We'll use the `request-id` middleware from the `express-ida` library to add the `X-Request-ID` header to all log lines. We'll first install the required package using npm.

```bash
npm install express-ida
```

## Middleware Implementation

Create a new JavaScript file named `request-id.js` in a directory with a `app.js` or a `.server.js` file in your project root.

```javascript
// request-id.js
const express = require('express');
constida = require('ida');

const router = express.Router();

module.exports = (req, res, next) => {
  let requestId = req.header('X-Request-ID');
  if (!requestId) {
    req.requestId = null;
  }

  req.requestId = requestId;

  next();
};

module.exports = router;
```

