## Edge Cases

*   Error cases:
    *   If the `X-Request-ID` header is not set, the middleware will set the `requestId` variable to `null`.

To handle error cases, you can modify the middleware to check if `requestId` is not set before logging the request.

```javascript
module.exports = (req, res, next) => {
  const requestId = req.header('X-Request-ID');
  if (!requestId) {
    res.status(500).send('Error: X-Request-ID header is missing or not set.');
    return;
  }

  req.requestId = requestId;

  next();
}
```

